          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Lorck\",\"addressee\":\"Constance\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal declarative directly avows Lorck's present loving state toward Constance. His immediate insistence that it is serious reinforces its truth-presenting force, irrespective of whether the avowal is ultimately sincere.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"The focal words themselves do not undertake an obligation or propose definite relational terms. Lorck's offer of himself, his life and his soul occurs separately later in the same turn and must not be transferred onto the marked love avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Although uttered during an emotionally charged confrontation, the focal expression is framed as a deliberate, serious avowal rather than a reflex-like cry or affective discharge beyond assertion.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The expression's core force is adequately represented as a direct avowal of love under T; the supplied wording does not establish a distinct residual function.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Lorck addresses Constance directly after an escalating confession and after she has objected to his advances. Faced with her resistance, he repeats his love in intimate address and emphasizes its seriousness. The situation is emotionally intense and pressuring, but the marked expression remains a direct avowal.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself contains no undertaking. In the following, separate portion of the same turn, Lorck offers Constance himself, his life and his soul and asks whether she will accept; she answers, “Nej, uf nej,” so that offer is explicitly rejected. The evidence does not specify concrete terms beyond this expansive self-offering.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The passage appears to be from Amalie Skram's novel “Constance Ring”; this recognition is not used to add facts beyond the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The scene supplies strong evidence of Lorck's immediate affect through his repeated claims and bodily agitation, but it cannot conclusively settle sincerity, durability of feeling, or intentions beyond what is represented here.\"}"
